      "content": "it's just constant. every single night. i just sit here and think about how much easier it would be if the physical version of me matched the version everyone else sees. they've already decided i'm a bad person, a nothing. it feels like i'm just waiting for my body to catch up to the fact that i'm already socially dead. is it even a tragedy if you're just finishing something that already happened?",
